# Sacrifice a kobold corpse at an altar of Khasrach, the orc god.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/sacrifice-goblinoid.keys 1
#
# The control for tools/keys/sacrifice-wildcard.keys. A kobold is a goblinoid
# (MA_GOBLINOID is orc OR goblin OR kobold, src/Values.cpp), so it matches
# row 1 of Khasrach's SACRIFICE_LIST -- MA_GOBLINOID SAC_ANGRY. Row 1 is
# BEFORE the first MA_ALL row, so the inc-upw.27 fix must not change this
# result at all:
#
#   both builds:  "Anger: Khasrach +1 (offensive sacrifice)."
#
# Measured on both sides on 2026-08-18 and identical. Without this control the
# wildcard script alone cannot tell "MA_ALL now matches" from "the loop now
# matches anything".
#
# Seed-locked for the same reasons as sacrifice-wildcard.keys; read that
# header first. The extra moves here (RIGHT*4 HOME UP*2) walk from the dwarf
# corpse to the kobold corpse.
#
# Khasrach has no text for MSG_BADSAC2, so the run also prints "Khasrach says
# something, but you aren't sure what it is!". That is a content gap in
# lib/religion.irh, not a fault in this script, and it predates the fix.

@include chargen.keys

END                 # walk to the dwarf corpse first, as the wildcard script
LEFT*5              # does, then on to the kobold corpse
RIGHT*4
HOME
UP*2

w                   # wizard mode; lowercase, see sacrifice-wildcard.keys
y
M                   # [M] Create Altar
"Khasrach"
ENTER

p                   # pray -- [abis]
s                   # ...sacrifice
@dump:offer            # so the check can prove WHICH corpse [w] is
w                   # [w] kobold corpse (on floor)

@dump:angry
@quit
